ing high risk locations...\nBeulah Water Intake, Northcreek Road county line to Red Mountain Camp\nand Northcreek Road from Red Mountain Camp to Beulah.","ends":"2026-08-27T18:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Custer, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d0b691cc2b76f65e9c0114699afe6dcdc4d91c1b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d0b691cc2b76f65e9c0114699afe6dcdc4d91c1b.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 27 at 5:27PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 527 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a cluster of strong\nthunderstorms over Walsenburg, or 35 miles northwest of Trinidad,\nmoving southeast at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and nickel size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nWalsenburg, La Veta, La Veta Pass, Spring Burn Scar north of Highway\n160, and northern Spring Burn Scar south of Highway 160 in Huerfano\ncounty.","ends":"2026-08-27T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Northern Sangre de Cristo Mountains Between 8500 And 11000 Ft; Southern Sangre De Cristo Mountains Between 7500 and 11000 Ft; Walsenburg Vicinity/Upper Huerfano River Basin Below 7500 Ft; Trinidad Vicinity/Western Las Animas County Below 7500 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea444a05646c86beb5ef657a19af9f510c07091.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea444a05646c86beb5ef657a19af9f510c07091.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 27 at 11:20AM MDT until August 27 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\nwill be possible over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres Burn Scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres Burn Scar should prepare for debris flows and stay up to date\nwith information from local authorities. Heavy rainfall could\ntrigger flash flooding of low-lying areas and debris flows in and\nnear recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel and Highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-27T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9798323cad440114383a15e74c30c9e9a07095b8.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9798323cad440114383a15e74c30c9e9a07095b8.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-27T23:29:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 272329 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 529 PM MDT Thu Aug 27 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers and storms into tonight. Flash flooding possible for the Aspen Acres burn scar, with a few severe storms possible along I-25. - Daily showers and storms will continue over the mountains each day into next week. The eastern plains will be a bit warmer and m","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-27T17:19:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 271719 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1119 AM MDT Thu Aug 27 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-281730- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawa